  "narrative": "These twelve results mostly strengthen the central conditional architecture and give clearer evidence that feature_063 is a candidate lowering marker once the two largest axes (feature_010 and feature_037) are removed. H163 is the decisive feature_063 contrast: within feature_010=0 and feature_037=0, the signed lowering estimate is 0.261 with lower bound 0.172, exceeding the 0.15 threshold; I accept this dataset-specific conditional contrast, but keep it active because the predictor is new and I request independent validation of H163. The broader marginal H148 remains unresolved because its lower bound crosses threshold and because context-specific tests are mixed. H153 is borderline: excluding feature_037 alone gives signed estimate 0.238 but lower bound 0.140, so threshold certainty is not established. H164 within feature_010=1 is not supported (point 0.102), but its upper bound reaches 0.391, so it remains unresolved rather than rejected, likely because of small exposed n and dilution. H150 and H154 reject negative feature_010 or feature_037 interaction hypotheses for feature_063: the signed intervals lie below the threshold and do not support a meaningful negative interaction in either context. This argues against a broad pattern in which feature_063 is primarily an interaction-specific signal on those two axes, while not excluding context-dependent heterogeneity elsewhere.\n\nThe feature_010 map becomes more robust. H151 confirms the large negative feature_010 contrast in jointly high feature_038/high feature_018 after removing feature_063-positive samples (0.822, lower 0.602). H160 and H161 confirm the symmetric feature_018-by-feature_038 interaction architecture after removing feature_063-positive samples, with signed estimates 0.765 and 0.538 and lower bounds above threshold. These support the central nonadditive architecture being identifiable beyond feature_063 composition, though the cells are modest and analyses remain unadjusted. H158 confirms the positive feature_010 contrast in high feature_036 after excluding feature_037 and feature_003 (0.557, lower 0.375), and H162 confirms feature_037's large lowering association after excluding feature_063 (0.845, lower 0.776). H155 and H157 further localize feature_003: a clean lowering contrast in high feature_036 with restrictive exclusions is accepted (0.382, lower 0.199), and the feature_018 modification of feature_003 within high feature_036 and feature_010=0 is accepted (0.504, lower 0.236), but the latter has small exposed cells and should be treated as a dataset-specific conditional association rather than a validated general interaction.\n\nFrom a critical-review perspective, the main cautions are multiplicity, small conditional cells, and unadjusted composition. Conditioning on predictors can reduce confounding by the strongest observed axes but can also restrict the population and induce non-collapsibility of subgroup contrasts. None of these comparisons establishes causality or biological generalizability; they are associations on a composite dependency score in this supplied dataset. I therefore request validation only for H163, the cleanest new-predictor contrast, because it addresses the largest remaining uncertainty: whether feature_063 is an independent lowering marker rather than an artifact of feature_010/feature_037 composition. The new proposals test feature_063 across high/low and non-high signature regions, test feature_010 and feature_037 after removing feature_063, and test whether feature_003 localization survives excluding feature_037.",
  "research_notes": "Updated dataset-specific map: feature_037 is a very large lowering association and remains large after excluding feature_063. feature_010 is positive in high feature_036 excluding feature_037/feature_003, but negative in joint-high feature_038/feature_018; this negative joint region and the symmetric interaction architecture survive exclusion of feature_063. feature_003 lowering remains strongly localized to high feature_036 and appears robust in restrictive high-feature_036 exclusions; the feature_018 modification is accepted but small-cell and conditional. feature_063 is now conditionally accepted within feature_010=0 and feature_037=0 (H163), with marginal H148 and feature_037-only H153 still threshold-uncertain; within feature_010=1 remains unresolved; interactions by feature_010 and feature_037 are not supported. feature_060 and feature_001 remain nulls. Validation budget is now used on H163. Next priorities: (1) feature_063 robustness across non-high and high feature_038/feature_018 regions after excluding feature_010/feature_037; (2) feature_010 positive map and joint-high reversal after removing feature_063 and feature_037; (3) feature_037 lowering after removing feature_063/feature_003; (4) feature_003 localization after removing feature_037. All remain unadjusted associations on a composite dependency score, not causal or external biological claims.",
